WEBVTT

00:00:03,950 --> 00:00:07,430
Hello everybody, this is Angie and if you've had

00:00:07,430 --> 00:00:09,510
thermography done at Conner's Clinic,

00:00:09,510 --> 00:00:12,750
you will most likely speak to me about your report.

00:00:12,750 --> 00:00:15,270
So this is a preview of what you can expect

00:00:15,270 --> 00:00:18,950
when we go over your thermography results.

00:00:18,950 --> 00:00:24,060
So we'll talk about what thermography is,

00:00:24,060 --> 00:00:26,780
scheduling your thermography review,

00:00:26,780 --> 00:00:29,260
so you'll want to make sure that you do that

00:00:29,260 --> 00:00:31,900
after you have your thermography scan.

00:00:31,900 --> 00:00:34,460
It's a 15 minute appointment with me.

00:00:34,900 --> 00:00:37,180
I'll send you a Zoom link for the appointment.

00:00:37,180 --> 00:00:39,220
We'll go over that in just a minute.

00:00:39,220 --> 00:00:41,300
We'll talk about what's included on the report,

00:00:41,300 --> 00:00:45,580
what the radiologist, what they base their findings on,

00:00:45,580 --> 00:00:47,700
important information on the report,

00:00:47,700 --> 00:00:49,140
we'll look at a sample report

00:00:49,140 --> 00:00:52,660
and we'll also talk about next steps.

00:00:52,660 --> 00:00:57,660
So thermography captures and records temperature variations

00:00:59,180 --> 00:01:03,340
on the skin, which is the largest organ of the body.

00:01:03,340 --> 00:01:07,340
The surface of the skin provides vital information

00:01:07,340 --> 00:01:12,340
that is directly influenced by complex metabolic

00:01:13,380 --> 00:01:17,540
and vascular activity below the surface of the skin.

00:01:17,540 --> 00:01:21,220
These patterns of activity can vary

00:01:21,220 --> 00:01:26,220
and intensity and distribution over each area of the body

00:01:26,220 --> 00:01:31,220
and that's represented by images with variation in colors.

00:01:32,140 --> 00:01:35,900
In looking at variations in skin temperature,

00:01:35,900 --> 00:01:40,900
we can see asymmetric abnormal or suspicious thermal patterns.

00:01:43,140 --> 00:01:46,620
These patterns may be recognized then by the interpreter

00:01:46,620 --> 00:01:52,960
as abnormal physiology or function or they may not.

00:01:53,440 --> 00:01:57,240
These findings may be able to contribute

00:01:57,240 --> 00:01:59,320
then to the decision making process

00:01:59,320 --> 00:02:03,160
regarding future therapy, maybe some additional testing

00:02:03,160 --> 00:02:05,040
that you might want to have done

00:02:05,040 --> 00:02:08,200
and possibly an eventual diagnosis.

00:02:08,200 --> 00:02:10,920
Thermography itself is not a diagnostic tool

00:02:10,920 --> 00:02:17,220
but it can give us hints about what may be going on.

00:02:17,220 --> 00:02:19,020
If you haven't already done so,

00:02:19,020 --> 00:02:20,980
you'll need to call the clinic to schedule

00:02:20,980 --> 00:02:22,960
your thermography review appointment.

00:02:22,960 --> 00:02:25,700
Again, this is about 15 minutes.

00:02:25,700 --> 00:02:27,780
Prior to your thermography review,

00:02:27,780 --> 00:02:31,460
you can look for an email from Connor's clinic.

00:02:31,460 --> 00:02:36,460
I will send you the Zoom link inside of that email.

00:02:36,460 --> 00:02:39,820
About five minutes before our appointment,

00:02:39,820 --> 00:02:42,460
while you're on your PC or Mac,

00:02:42,460 --> 00:02:45,060
you can click on the link in that email that I send you

00:02:45,060 --> 00:02:47,300
to join the web conference.

00:02:47,300 --> 00:02:51,420
This is what the body of the email will look like,

00:02:51,420 --> 00:02:54,660
the list the time and date of our appointment

00:02:54,660 --> 00:02:57,500
that I scheduled, that you scheduled,

00:02:57,500 --> 00:03:00,460
and the link to click on,

00:03:00,460 --> 00:03:04,580
if you've not downloaded Zoom to your device

00:03:05,500 --> 00:03:07,380
prior to this appointment,

00:03:07,380 --> 00:03:10,980
just ask you to click on this link about five minutes

00:03:10,980 --> 00:03:12,220
before our appointment.

00:03:13,180 --> 00:03:16,980
You may need to then download the app onto your computer,

00:03:16,980 --> 00:03:19,660
which you'll just follow through some prompts

00:03:19,660 --> 00:03:21,900
to download it onto your device

00:03:21,900 --> 00:03:24,340
and then you'll be able to click

00:03:24,340 --> 00:03:29,790
to be able to join in on our meeting.

00:03:29,790 --> 00:03:30,910
And then you'll wanna just make sure

00:03:30,910 --> 00:03:33,110
that your computer volume is turned up

00:03:33,110 --> 00:03:37,030
so that you can hear me and I can hear you.

00:03:37,030 --> 00:03:41,030
We won't see each other, but you will see my screen

00:03:41,030 --> 00:03:45,630
that shows your report.

00:03:45,630 --> 00:03:47,330
When you get your report,

00:03:47,330 --> 00:03:50,290
it'll have all of the information

00:03:50,290 --> 00:03:54,410
that you provided on your thermography intake form.

00:03:54,410 --> 00:03:57,970
It'll contain the radiologist's interpretation

00:03:57,970 --> 00:04:02,410
of the images and recommendations for next steps

00:04:02,410 --> 00:04:05,130
if they are recommending any.

00:04:05,130 --> 00:04:07,210
For breast scans,

00:04:07,210 --> 00:04:12,210
each woman will receive a grading or classification

00:04:14,480 --> 00:04:19,460
identifying what level of risk you're currently at.

00:04:19,460 --> 00:04:23,460
The report also has an explanation of thermography

00:04:23,460 --> 00:04:25,380
similar to what we just talked about.

00:04:25,380 --> 00:04:31,580
A color scale and of course your thermography images.

00:04:31,580 --> 00:04:33,980
So what are the findings based on?

00:04:33,980 --> 00:04:36,580
You're based on your thermography intake information

00:04:36,580 --> 00:04:38,940
that you provided on the form

00:04:38,940 --> 00:04:42,500
of the Connors Clinic Thermography intake form.

00:04:42,500 --> 00:04:45,740
Your diagnosis is included on that

00:04:45,740 --> 00:04:49,260
as well as the health history that you provide on that form,

00:04:49,260 --> 00:04:51,740
your clinical concerns, your family history

00:04:51,740 --> 00:04:54,740
and of course findings are based on the images.

00:04:55,740 --> 00:04:58,940
The radiologists that read these images

00:04:58,940 --> 00:05:03,300
do not have, they're not privy to what we do here

00:05:03,300 --> 00:05:05,620
at Connors Clinic with our patients.

00:05:05,620 --> 00:05:10,820
They don't know about the findings with the exams

00:05:10,820 --> 00:05:13,260
or the therapies or protocols.

00:05:13,260 --> 00:05:17,740
So all they know is the thermography intake information

00:05:17,740 --> 00:05:21,650
and your images.

00:05:21,650 --> 00:05:24,730
When we take a look at a sample report in just a minute,

00:05:24,730 --> 00:05:29,170
you'll see information that is highlighted.

00:05:29,170 --> 00:05:34,170
This is my highlighting and I like to go in and look

00:05:35,290 --> 00:05:37,010
just prior to our appointment.

00:05:37,010 --> 00:05:40,210
I will go in and look at your thermography report

00:05:40,210 --> 00:05:42,170
and your images and I'll go through

00:05:42,170 --> 00:05:43,890
and I will highlight the things that I want

00:05:43,890 --> 00:05:46,450
to make sure that I point out to you.

00:05:46,450 --> 00:05:49,010
You'll wanna make sure to read the rest of your report

00:05:49,010 --> 00:05:50,050
when we get done talking

00:05:50,050 --> 00:05:51,570
and of course if you have any questions

00:05:51,570 --> 00:05:53,370
about anything after that don't hesitate

00:05:53,370 --> 00:05:54,370
to reach out to me.

00:05:56,490 --> 00:06:00,690
And again, you will receive a grading classification

00:06:00,690 --> 00:06:06,150
if you had a breast scan done.

00:06:06,150 --> 00:06:12,720
So let's take a look at the report.

00:06:12,800 --> 00:06:19,530
When we start our meeting I will have images up on one side

00:06:20,370 --> 00:06:23,730
and your report up on the other side

00:06:23,730 --> 00:06:27,170
so that I can be going over your images

00:06:27,170 --> 00:06:31,940
while we look at your report.

00:06:31,940 --> 00:06:35,820
Health history that you provided is located here.

00:06:35,820 --> 00:06:40,290
The thermographic interpretation is here

00:06:40,290 --> 00:06:43,050
and they typically start at the top of the body.

00:06:43,050 --> 00:06:45,290
So the first section is the head and neck section

00:06:45,290 --> 00:06:47,490
and the first thing that they mentioned

00:06:47,490 --> 00:06:51,530
that I want to point out to patients when I see this

00:06:51,530 --> 00:06:54,050
is hypothermia around the mouth.

00:06:54,050 --> 00:06:59,050
When we see this unless a patient has just had dental

00:06:59,050 --> 00:07:04,050
work done or know that they've had some irritation

00:07:04,850 --> 00:07:08,050
to the gums or teeth.

00:07:09,810 --> 00:07:13,530
When we see this hypothermia around the mouth

00:07:13,530 --> 00:07:18,530
that is something we want to nip in the bud.

00:07:20,930 --> 00:07:25,330
You can see on the report here that the radiologist

00:07:26,050 --> 00:07:31,050
noted that this hypothermia is most likely consistent

00:07:31,050 --> 00:07:35,210
with some degree of what might be subclinical dental,

00:07:35,210 --> 00:07:36,810
periodontal irritation.

00:07:38,010 --> 00:07:39,610
Many patients are asymptomatic.

00:07:39,610 --> 00:07:42,330
They don't have any pain in their mouth

00:07:42,330 --> 00:07:44,890
or know of any infection.

00:07:44,890 --> 00:07:47,850
But this is one thing that we like about thermography

00:07:47,850 --> 00:07:50,130
is it can give us hints as to what's going on in the body.

00:07:50,130 --> 00:07:54,370
So we recommend when we see this our tooth

00:07:54,490 --> 00:07:56,010
and gum oil.

00:07:56,010 --> 00:07:57,810
It comes in a dropper bottle.

00:07:57,810 --> 00:08:02,810
It's about 70% black cumin seed oil and 30% oregano oil.

00:08:04,770 --> 00:08:06,610
And it's a good preventive.

00:08:06,610 --> 00:08:11,450
A good antibacterial will help fight infection.

00:08:11,450 --> 00:08:15,490
We don't want periodontal irritation,

00:08:15,490 --> 00:08:18,170
inflammation to turn into periodontal disease

00:08:18,170 --> 00:08:22,450
that can lead to other issues in the body with the heart.

00:08:22,450 --> 00:08:27,730
And it can lead to cancers as well.

00:08:27,730 --> 00:08:29,410
So that is common.

00:08:29,410 --> 00:08:34,710
We may find that on your report as well.

00:08:34,710 --> 00:08:37,590
Honest persons report, there's also increased activity

00:08:37,590 --> 00:08:42,550
at the front of the neck, which the radiologist noted

00:08:42,550 --> 00:08:46,910
might be suggestive of some degree of thyroid dysfunction

00:08:47,950 --> 00:08:49,990
correlate clinically.

00:08:49,990 --> 00:08:56,690
So what that means is you might want to have that checked out

00:08:56,690 --> 00:08:59,770
and you can have that checked out with your doctor

00:08:59,770 --> 00:09:04,770
with blood test that can do a thyroid workup

00:09:04,850 --> 00:09:08,010
and see how your numbers look there.

00:09:08,010 --> 00:09:13,010
You can also set up an appointment with us to chat about that.

00:09:13,010 --> 00:09:15,650
We may be able to do kinesiology to test

00:09:15,650 --> 00:09:17,970
and see if there is anything going on with the thyroid

00:09:17,970 --> 00:09:20,410
or if that's coming up with kinesiology,

00:09:20,410 --> 00:09:25,560
we can help address that as well.

00:09:25,560 --> 00:09:28,600
Honest persons report, there are no findings

00:09:28,600 --> 00:09:32,880
to indicate significant carotid artery dysfunction,

00:09:33,760 --> 00:09:37,720
but there is a slight increase at the base

00:09:37,720 --> 00:09:42,720
of the right carotid artery, which is this area here.

00:09:42,800 --> 00:09:45,160
That might be suggestive or be related

00:09:45,160 --> 00:09:48,680
to systemic inflammation or elevated CRP levels.

00:09:48,680 --> 00:09:50,840
CRP stands for C-reactive protein,

00:09:50,840 --> 00:09:52,880
that's an inflammatory marker.

00:09:52,920 --> 00:09:56,600
So this is not uncommon in inflammation,

00:09:56,600 --> 00:10:01,600
systemic inflammation often leads to disease.

00:10:02,120 --> 00:10:08,810
So this is not uncommon to see with our patients that come in.

00:10:08,810 --> 00:10:12,610
And then in the breast section, this person

00:10:13,930 --> 00:10:18,930
does have some slight areas of thermic and hyperthermic activity

00:10:19,730 --> 00:10:24,730
to the central and peripheral regions of both breasts.

00:10:28,490 --> 00:10:33,490
So centrally located throughout this area here

00:10:35,210 --> 00:10:41,650
and to the sides, some slight hyperthermia here.

00:10:44,420 --> 00:10:49,420
And they do not appear suspicious, but should be monitored.

00:10:50,420 --> 00:10:54,420
By lateral underarm hyperthermia,

00:10:54,420 --> 00:10:59,420
they can tell by the patterns that this is consistent

00:11:00,220 --> 00:11:02,540
with lymphatic congestion.

00:11:02,540 --> 00:11:05,540
For our patients that have come into the clinic

00:11:05,540 --> 00:11:10,180
with our full program, our full plan patients,

00:11:10,180 --> 00:11:14,940
you spent two days here, and we on day two

00:11:14,940 --> 00:11:17,900
went over your three-ring binder

00:11:17,900 --> 00:11:20,020
and talked about some home exercises.

00:11:20,020 --> 00:11:24,660
One of those sheets talks about lymphatic exercises.

00:11:24,660 --> 00:11:28,780
So this is where I would probably refer patients

00:11:28,780 --> 00:11:32,540
to that sheet if we haven't already talked about it

00:11:32,540 --> 00:11:34,260
just to revisit that.

00:11:34,260 --> 00:11:39,260
And I would suggest that the patient continues

00:11:39,620 --> 00:11:44,620
or starts to do one or more of those lymphatic exercises

00:11:44,860 --> 00:11:50,530
to help keep lymph moving.

00:11:50,530 --> 00:11:52,970
In the breast section, if it's a good scan,

00:11:52,970 --> 00:11:56,010
you'll see words like this that the study is suitable

00:11:56,010 --> 00:11:59,490
to be archived and compared with a repeat study in three months.

00:11:59,490 --> 00:12:03,050
So the repeat study in three months gives us a comparison.

00:12:03,050 --> 00:12:05,010
So we have these first set of images

00:12:05,010 --> 00:12:07,690
and in three months when you come back

00:12:07,690 --> 00:12:11,890
for your follow-up scan or your baseline scan,

00:12:11,890 --> 00:12:15,050
they will compare the images from that scan

00:12:15,050 --> 00:12:20,050
to the original scan and be able to then give a recommendation

00:12:22,610 --> 00:12:26,290
as to whether or not you need to have

00:12:26,290 --> 00:12:29,090
some further monitoring done on a more regular basis

00:12:29,090 --> 00:12:33,450
or if things are changing, if they notice

00:12:33,450 --> 00:12:38,450
that patterns are changing or if hypothermia is increasing

00:12:38,930 --> 00:12:42,690
or maybe there's some vascular patterns

00:12:42,690 --> 00:12:47,370
that indicate there may be some developing pathology,

00:12:49,770 --> 00:12:54,770
they'll be able to note that on the three month baseline scan

00:12:54,810 --> 00:12:59,330
and if not, then if things look just like this

00:12:59,330 --> 00:13:01,610
and don't appear to be changing,

00:13:01,610 --> 00:13:05,090
then typically after that baseline scan

00:13:05,090 --> 00:13:08,570
unless a woman feels any additional lumps

00:13:08,570 --> 00:13:10,770
or starts having any dimpling of the scan

00:13:10,930 --> 00:13:15,330
or some other symptoms, it's okay typically to wait

00:13:15,330 --> 00:13:22,540
and then have tests done, another scan done in about a year.

00:13:22,700 --> 00:13:27,700
One other thing that I notice a lot in the thermography reports

00:13:28,220 --> 00:13:37,470
is something like this indicates some degree of

00:13:39,350 --> 00:13:42,910
or maybe indicative of or, you know,

00:13:42,950 --> 00:13:46,150
and fervidge like that so they can't say specifically

00:13:46,150 --> 00:13:51,150
what these thermal patterns are, they can only say that

00:13:52,590 --> 00:13:55,150
this is what it looks like to us, it could be this,

00:13:55,150 --> 00:13:59,030
it could be that so, and then again they may recommend

00:13:59,030 --> 00:14:04,040
that you get it checked out further.

00:14:04,040 --> 00:14:07,280
Many times we see this as well.

00:14:08,600 --> 00:14:13,080
hypothermia consistent with myofacial inflammation,

00:14:13,080 --> 00:14:16,100
lymphatic congestion and or muscular tension.

00:14:16,100 --> 00:14:19,620
That is very common to see on thermography reports.

00:14:19,620 --> 00:14:22,700
Myofascial inflammation refers to inflammation

00:14:22,700 --> 00:14:24,220
of the connective tissue.

00:14:24,220 --> 00:14:28,040
Connective tissue is weaved all throughout our bodies

00:14:28,040 --> 00:14:32,460
from head to toe and we see this quite a bit.

00:14:32,460 --> 00:14:35,940
Lymphatic congestion again, just want to point

00:14:35,940 --> 00:14:38,620
to those lymphatic exercises again

00:14:38,620 --> 00:14:40,020
and then muscular tension.

00:14:40,020 --> 00:14:42,380
We all carry some degree of muscular tension.

00:14:42,380 --> 00:14:45,740
So if we see a lot of that scattered throughout the report,

00:14:45,740 --> 00:14:49,780
I may suggest that the patient does some relaxation techniques,

00:14:49,780 --> 00:14:52,940
get some massage, something to help relax.

00:14:52,940 --> 00:15:00,240
A hot tub, you may soak in some ebbs and salts would be good.

00:15:00,240 --> 00:15:07,240
In the abdomen, they mention here that there is some

00:15:07,240 --> 00:15:14,480
hyperthermic activity around the belly button area

00:15:14,480 --> 00:15:18,400
which may indicate some element of gastrointestinal

00:15:18,400 --> 00:15:20,600
autonomic neural activity and they're

00:15:20,600 --> 00:15:27,320
suggesting a clinical evaluation for their investigation

00:15:27,320 --> 00:15:34,760
to find out what these patterns might be correlated with

00:15:34,760 --> 00:15:39,780
to tie them together with any symptoms.

00:15:39,780 --> 00:15:42,540
And then on the report, there is always a discussion section

00:15:42,540 --> 00:15:47,180
which typically recaps some of the things

00:15:47,180 --> 00:15:53,900
that are important on the report and then a follow-up.

00:15:53,900 --> 00:16:00,260
And all initial breast scans will say something like this

00:16:00,260 --> 00:16:04,220
that follow-up breast imaging is recommended in three months

00:16:04,220 --> 00:16:06,580
to establish a baseline before continuing

00:16:06,580 --> 00:16:09,620
with annual comparative studies.

00:16:09,620 --> 00:16:16,380
And here is where the classification or the grade is listed.

00:16:16,380 --> 00:16:19,020
Each breast will have its own.

00:16:19,020 --> 00:16:26,540
And in this case, the grading is at low risk for both left

00:16:26,540 --> 00:16:28,340
and right breast.

00:16:28,340 --> 00:16:30,220
There is a classification key here,

00:16:30,220 --> 00:16:37,560
so a patient can read more about their grade.

00:16:37,560 --> 00:16:39,440
As you scroll down your report, you'll

00:16:39,440 --> 00:16:45,040
see information about their procedure, protocols,

00:16:45,040 --> 00:16:57,030
what normal findings and abnormal findings consist of.

00:16:57,030 --> 00:17:01,150
So you can use this information when you're talking

00:17:01,150 --> 00:17:07,390
with us or with your other practitioners

00:17:07,390 --> 00:17:10,550
for their testing may be suggested.

00:17:10,550 --> 00:17:14,750
And thermography is especially with breast health.

00:17:14,750 --> 00:17:18,590
It's good to monitor over time.

00:17:18,590 --> 00:17:22,750
If desired, of course, you can set up an appointment with us

00:17:22,750 --> 00:17:31,110
to talk about anything that is found on your thermography imaging

00:17:31,110 --> 00:17:35,110
report that you might want to have checked out further.

00:17:35,110 --> 00:17:36,830
You can talk about that.

00:17:36,830 --> 00:17:39,190
We may be able to do some kinesiology testing

00:17:39,190 --> 00:17:42,830
to see if it comes up with kinesiology.

00:17:42,830 --> 00:17:46,670
And repeat, full body scans are not typically done,

00:17:46,670 --> 00:17:52,590
but we do repeat breast scans.

00:17:52,590 --> 00:17:55,310
We can monitor breast health over time,

00:17:55,310 --> 00:18:06,270
but there are just too many things in the body that could change.

00:18:06,270 --> 00:18:10,990
And breast health is what we really want to monitor.

00:18:10,990 --> 00:18:15,310
We can, you know, if you wanted to have a whole upper body

00:18:15,310 --> 00:18:19,990
and breast scan done to see if the hypothermia around your mouth

00:18:19,990 --> 00:18:25,030
has decreased because you've been using the tooth and gum oil.

00:18:25,030 --> 00:18:29,550
If you want to just satisfy your curiosity that way,

00:18:29,550 --> 00:18:34,870
we certainly could, but it isn't necessary.

00:18:34,870 --> 00:18:39,350
So we do repeat breast scans only typically.

00:18:39,350 --> 00:18:44,110
And then when we are done talking over our Zoom appointment,

00:18:44,110 --> 00:18:47,350
I will be sure to email your report to you

00:18:47,350 --> 00:18:51,430
so that you have a copy of it.

00:18:51,430 --> 00:18:54,550
So I thank you very much for listening,

00:18:54,550 --> 00:18:58,350
and I hope that this preview has been helpful for you,

00:18:58,350 --> 00:19:01,790
and I'm sure I will talk to you soon.

00:19:01,790 --> 00:19:03,430
Thank you.

